{"name":"Ice Age","hex":"#c6e4e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ice Age","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of ice age."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ice_Age"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ice age","blocks":[{"text":"An ice age is a period of time when decreased temperature of Earth's surface and atmosphere results in the prolonged presence or expansion of continental alpine glaciers and polar ice caps. The term is applied in several different senses to very long and comparatively short periods of cooling. An ice age may consist of numerous sub-periods where the global temperature and glaciation fluctuates, with the colder periods called glacials, and relatively warmer periods called interglacials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/IceAgeEarth.jpg/330px-IceAgeEarth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_age","wikidata":"Q49367"},{"title":"Late Cenozoic Ice Age","blocks":[{"text":"The Late Cenozoic Ice Age, or Antarctic Glaciation, began 34 million years ago at the Eocene-Oligocene Boundary and is ongoing. It is Earth's current ice age or icehouse period. Its beginning is marked by the formation of the Antarctic ice sheets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Pyrotherium_romeroi_e.jpg/330px-Pyrotherium_romeroi_e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Cenozoic_Ice_Age","wikidata":"Q56926766"},{"title":"Ice Age (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Ice Age is an American media franchise created by Michael J. Wilson, co-developed and based on an idea by Lori Forte. The franchise, centering on a group of mammals surviving the Pleistocene ice age, consists of computer-animated films, short films, TV specials and a series of video games. The first five films were produced by Blue Sky Studios, a subsidiary of 20th Century Fox Animation, and distributed by its then-parent company 20th Century Fox. The series features the voices of Ray Romano, John Leguizamo, Denis Leary, and Chris Wedge across all films, with Queen Latifah, Seann William Scott, Josh Peck, Simon Pegg, Wanda Sykes, Keke Palmer, and Jennifer Lopez joining the main cast in subsequent films. The films center mainly on the adventures of \"the Herd,\" which since the first film consists of at least woolly mammoth Manny (Romano), ground sloth Sid (Leguizamo), and Smilodon Diego (Leary). The franchise also features mostly independent plotlines involving a dialogue-free saber-toothed squirrel named Scrat (Wedge), who ends up in misadventures from trying to retrieve and bury his acorns, the latter act creates a chain of events that sets up the various adventures of the protagonists."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Iceage-logo.svg/330px-Iceage-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice_Age_(franchise)","wikidata":"Q943532"},{"title":"Ice","blocks":[{"text":"Ice is water that is frozen into a solid state, typically forming at or below temperatures of 0 °C, 32 °F, or 273.15 K. It occurs naturally on Earth, on other planets, in Oort cloud objects, and as interstellar ice. As a naturally occurring crystalline inorganic solid with an ordered structure, ice is considered to be a mineral. Depending on the presence of impurities such as particles of soil or bubbles of air, it can appear transparent or a more or less opaque bluish-white color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg/330px-Ice_Block%2C_Canal_Park%2C_Duluth_%2832752478892%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ice","wikidata":"Q23392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Haukalivatnet.JPG/500px-Haukalivatnet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Haukalivatnet.JPG/1280px-Haukalivatnet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Haukalivatnet.JPG/500px-Haukalivatnet.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haukalivatnet lake (50 meters—164 feet—above sea level) where Jens Esmark in 1823 discovered similarities to moraines near existing glaciers in the high mountains","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHaukalivatnet.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg/500px-GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg/1280px-GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg/500px-GlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Timeline of glaciations, shown in blue","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlaciationsinEarthExistancelicenced_annotated.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/EisrandlagenNorddeutschland.png/330px-EisrandlagenNorddeutschland.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/EisrandlagenNorddeutschland.png/330px-EisrandlagenNorddeutschland.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_